- [ ] 3. In `src/tickets.js`, add `rateTicket` after `reopenTicket` and before `mustGet`:

      ```js
      function rateTicket(store, id, score, { now = new Date() } = {}) {
        if (!Number.isInteger(score) || score < 1 || score > 5) throw new Error('score must be a whole number from 1 to 5');
        const t = mustGet(store, id);
        if (t.status !== STATUS.RESOLVED) throw new Error(`cannot rate a ${t.status} ticket`);
        if (store.getRating(id)) throw new Error(`ticket ${id} already has a rating`);
        store.addRating(id, { score, rated_at: now.toISOString() });
        if (score <= 2 && t.owner_id) notifyAgent(store, t.owner_id, { type: 'low_csat_rating', ticketId: id, score });
        return store.getRating(id);
      }
      ```
      and add `rateTicket` to the `module.exports` line.
      Evidence: `npm test` — same failures as before (nothing in `portal.js` calls this yet).
- [ ] 4. In `src/portal.js`, change the import line from
      `const { STATUS, createTicket } = require('./tickets');` to
      `const { STATUS, createTicket, rateTicket: rateTicketById } = require('./tickets');`, add
      after `reply`:

      ```js
      function rateTicket(store, customer, id, score, { now = new Date() } = {}) {
        const t = getMyTicket(store, customer, id);
        if (!t) return null;
        return rateTicketById(store, id, score, { now });
      }
      ```
      and add `rateTicket` to the `module.exports` line.
      Evidence: `npm test` — all tests pass, including the six new ones.
- [ ] 5. In `docs/glossary.md`, add after the **Organisation** entry:
      `**Rating.** A customer's 1–5 score on a resolved ticket, given at most once. A score of 1
      or 2 notifies the ticket's owner by email.`
      Evidence: visual check — the line reads correctly in the rendered file.
- [ ] 6. In `README.md`, change the `src/portal.js` bullet from `` `src/portal.js`: what a
      customer can do from the portal. `` to `` `src/portal.js`: what a customer can do from the
      portal, including rating a resolved ticket. ``
      Evidence: visual check.
- [ ] 7. Commit: `git add src/store.js src/tickets.js src/portal.js test/tickets.test.js
      docs/glossary.md README.md && git commit -m "let a customer rate a resolved ticket"`.

## Exit criteria

- `npm test` green, all six new tests plus every pre-existing test passing.
- Independent review (`bk-review`, different author) before `bk-ship`, because this phase adds
  behaviour to `portal.js`, the tenant-scoping boundary; the "other organisation" test above is
  the regression test the kit's security baseline requires for that boundary.

## Risks

- `t.owner_id` can be null if a ticket was resolved without ever being assigned (the existing
  `resolveTicket` does not require an owner). The `&& t.owner_id` guard in step 3 means the
  rating is still stored and the low-score path is simply skipped, rather than throwing — this
  was not in the acceptance criteria and is called out here as the chosen behaviour, not left
  implicit.

